@program gtk3-text-input-test
@compositor gnome
# As wl-im-windows.keys, through GNOME's IBus (hime-ibus), which learns the
# focused application from GNOME Shell's replies to its portal: each
# application has an input state of its own (each window of the test,
# which has no .desktop file, is an application of its own for GNOME
# Shell).  Control+Space in the first window leaves a second one in
# Chinese, and the first one is still in English when it gets the focus
# back.
C-<space> x @check @exec gtk3-text-input-test:a:<space> y @check
